nt of about one to two  percent to show you're serious about  buying this will go into an escrow  account held by a third party until the  transaction's complete in this final  stage you'll likely need a lawyer to  help you do some paperwork make sure  you're getting the best deal and stay  out of any legal trouble with the help  of your lawyer and your real estate  agent you'll want to conduct some  serious inspections of the property to  make sure there are no defects or other  problems once the checks are done your  financing is cleared and you've signed  on the dotted line the house is yours  and you can stop scrolling on that phone  at least for houses good luck
 

